**Goal** — Add the environment-resolved chat theme without changing the current screen.

**Motivation** — The slice 1 acceptance test (brainstorm and spec-review the slice 2 design inside `nax chat`) waits on this redesign.

**Approach** — `theme.ts` resolves one `ChatTheme` from the environment and the chalk colour level.

Colour table (levels 2 and 3 use the hex value; level 1 uses the named colour; level 0, `NO_COLOR` set to any non-empty value, or `TERM=dumb` gives every token `undefined` and `color: false`):

| Token | Dark | Light | 16-colour |
|---|---|---|---|
| accent | `#2bb5a3` | `#0f7f71` | `cyan` |
| muted | `#7d8f8c` | `#6b7b78` | `gray` |
| success | `#4cc38a` | `#1f8a55` | `green` |
| warning | `#e5b84a` | `#9a6b00` | `yellow` |
| danger | `#f0625b` | `#c23a33` | `red` |
| diffAdd | `#12352a` | `#d7f2e3` | undefined |
| diffRemove | `#3d1a1c` | `#fadcdb` | undefined |
| userBand | `#17221f` | `#eaf1ef` | undefined |
| border | `#2a3a37` | `#c7d3d0` | `gray` |
| borderFocus | `#2bb5a3` | `#0f7f71` | `cyan` |
| syntaxKeyword | `#d19af2` | `#8a3fbf` | `magenta` |
| syntaxString | `#9ccc8a` | `#2f7d32` | `green` |
| syntaxComment | `#6f817e` | `#7a8a87` | `gray` |
| syntaxNumber | `#e5a46c` | `#a65a14` | `yellow` |
| syntaxTitle | `#7cc4f0` | `#1f6fae` | `blue` |

`background` is `"light"` when `COLORFGBG` is set and its last `;`-separated field is `7` or `15`; otherwise `"dark"`. Glyphs are the Unicode set (`⏺ ⎿ ❯ ⏵ ⏵⏵ ※ ⚠ ✗ ✻ … ─ ┌ │ └`, spinner `· ✢ ✳ ✶ ✻ ✽`) unless `NAX_ASCII` is `"1"` or the first non-empty of `LC_ALL`, `LC_CTYPE`, `LANG` does not match `/utf-?8/i`; then the ASCII set (`* | > > >> - ! x * ... - + | +`, spinner `- \ | /`). With no locale variable set, the Unicode set is used.

**Scope** — In: new theme module and unit tests. Out: styled-line rendering (US-002), CLI environment wiring (US-020), changing the run TUI.

**Interface** —
```ts
export type ChatColorToken =
  | "accent" | "muted" | "success" | "warning" | "danger"
  | "diffAdd" | "diffRemove" | "userBand" | "border" | "borderFocus"
  | "syntaxKeyword" | "syntaxString" | "syntaxComment" | "syntaxNumber" | "syntaxTitle";
export interface ChatGlyphs {
  readonly bullet: string; readonly result: string; readonly pointer: string;
  readonly modeGuarded: string; readonly modeFull: string; readonly notice: string;
  readonly warning: string; readonly error: string; readonly thinking: string;
  readonly ellipsis: string; readonly rule: string;
  readonly codeTop: string; readonly codeSide: string; readonly codeBottom: string;
  readonly spinner: readonly string[];
}
export interface ChatTheme {
  readonly color: boolean;
  readonly background: "dark" | "light";
  /** Ink colour strings; undefined = terminal default (and no background for bg tokens). */
  readonly colors: Readonly<Record<ChatColorToken, string | undefined>>;
  readonly glyphs: ChatGlyphs;
}
export function resolveChatTheme(input: {
  env: Readonly<Record<string, string | undefined>>;
  colorLevel: 0 | 1 | 2 | 3;
}): ChatTheme;
```

**Goal** — Add the shared styled-line primitive and safe display text utilities.

**Motivation** — The slice 1 acceptance test (brainstorm and spec-review the slice 2 design inside `nax chat`) waits on this redesign.

**Approach** — `styled-line.tsx` defines the one rendering primitive every model produces: a `StyledLine` is an array of `Span`s; `StyledLineView` renders one line with the theme's colours.

Every width, wrap and truncation in the models below is measured with `displayWidth`, and a `width` below `MIN_LAYOUT_WIDTH` is treated as `MIN_LAYOUT_WIDTH`. Every text that comes from the session, a tool, an MCP server or the host (reply, thinking, preview, tool input, notices, listings) passes through `sanitizeText` before it becomes span text, so a tool preview containing `\u001b[?1049l` cannot leave the alternate screen.

**Scope** — In: span rendering, plain text extraction, Bun display-column measurement and control-sequence sanitising. Out: markdown (US-007/008), transcript layout (US-009..011), mounting in ChatApp (US-020).

**Interface** —
```ts
export interface Span {
  readonly text: string;
  readonly color?: ChatColorToken;
  readonly background?: ChatColorToken;
  readonly bold?: boolean;
  readonly italic?: boolean;
}
export type StyledLine = readonly Span[];
export function plainText(line: StyledLine): string;
/** Terminal display columns (Bun.stringWidth): CJK and emoji count 2. */
export function displayWidth(text: string): number;
/** Strips ANSI/OSC escape sequences, C0 controls except "\n", and DEL (0x7f); a tab becomes two spaces. */
export function sanitizeText(text: string): string;
export const MIN_LAYOUT_WIDTH = 10;
```
`StyledLineView` renders one line with the theme's colours.

**Goal** — Add the immutable event-to-transcript reducer beside the legacy transcript.

**Motivation** — The slice 1 acceptance test (brainstorm and spec-review the slice 2 design inside `nax chat`) waits on this redesign.

**Approach** — `transcript-model.ts` holds the entry union and a pure reducer `reduceTranscript(entries, event)`. Entries are immutable; an update returns a new object for the changed entry only, so unchanged entries keep their identity (the layout cache in US-010 depends on this).

Reducer rules: `text_delta` appends to the last entry when it is a `reply` of the same turn, else adds a `reply`. `thinking_delta` appends to the open (no `endedAt`) `thinking` entry of its turn, else adds one with `startedAt = event.at`. Any `text_delta`, `tool_call` or `turn_end` of a turn sets `endedAt = event.at` on that turn's open thinking entry. A `tool_call` whose `metadata.subagentTask` is set becomes a `ToolChild` of the most recent running `nax-agents__run` entry whose `input.task` equals it; with no such parent it is added as a top-level tool entry. `tool_result` updates the matching entry (or child) by `turnId` + `callId` (child: by `callId` within the parent) to `ok`/`error`, and on a top-level entry also sets `preview` and `endedAt`. `turn_end` with status `errored` and an `error` adds an `error` entry `"<code>: <message>"`; with status `cancelled` it adds `interrupted`. `compaction` adds the notice `conversation compacted`. Every other event returns the input array unchanged (same reference).

**Scope** — In: new immutable model/reducer and unit tests. Out: replacing Transcript.tsx/appendChatEvent (US-020/028), tool formatting (US-005/006), rendering (US-009..011).

**Interface** —
```ts
export interface ToolChild {
  readonly callId: string; readonly name: string; readonly input: unknown;
  readonly status: "running" | "ok" | "error";
}
export type TranscriptEntry =
  | { kind: "welcome"; skills: number; commands: number; agents: number; mcpServers: number; mcpConnected: number }
  | { kind: "user"; text: string }
  | { kind: "reply"; turnId: string; text: string }
  | { kind: "thinking"; turnId: string; text: string; startedAt: string; endedAt?: string }
  | { kind: "tool"; turnId: string; callId: string; name: string; input: unknown;
      startedAt: string; status: "running" | "ok" | "error"; preview?: string;
      endedAt?: string; children: readonly ToolChild[] }
  | { kind: "notice"; text: string }
  | { kind: "warning"; text: string }
  | { kind: "error"; text: string }
  | { kind: "listing"; title: string; text: string }
  | { kind: "interrupted" };
export function reduceTranscript(entries: readonly TranscriptEntry[], event: SessionEvent): readonly TranscriptEntry[];
```

**Goal** — Add a pure tool-card model for identity and running/error states.

**Motivation** — The slice 1 acceptance test (brainstorm and spec-review the slice 2 design inside `nax chat`) waits on this redesign.

**Approach** — `tool-card.ts`, pure:
- `toolTitle`: `nax-agents__run` -> `Agent`, `nax-skills__load` -> `Skill`, any other name unchanged.
- `arg`: Read/Write/Edit/Delete -> `input.path`; Bash -> first line of `input.command`; Grep -> `"<pattern>"` plus `, <path>` when `input.path` is a string; Glob -> `input.pattern`; Git -> `input.subcommand`; Agent -> `<agent>: <task>`; Skill -> `input.name`; any other tool, or a missing/non-string field -> undefined. Longer than `TOOL_ARG_LIMIT` characters -> the first `TOOL_ARG_LIMIT` characters plus the theme-independent `…`. Line breaks in the value become spaces.
- `tone`: `running` while running, `success` on ok, `danger` on error.
- `summary` while running: empty, except Agent, whose summary is its children as muted `Title(arg)` lines, the last `CHILD_PREVIEW_LINES` only, preceded by a muted `+N more tool uses` line when more exist.
- `summary` on error: the first non-empty preview line, tone `danger` (`"failed"` when the preview is empty or absent).

**Scope** — In: toolTitle, argument derivation/truncation, tone, running/error summaries, shared model types/constants and tests. Out: ok summaries/diffLines/collapse behavior (US-006), styled layout (US-010). Subagent tokens are not shown on the Agent card; only tool-use count and duration, because nested usage is not forwarded to the transcript.

**Interface** —
```ts
export interface CardLine { readonly text: string; readonly tone: "plain" | "muted" | "danger" }
export interface DiffLine { readonly sign: "-" | "+" | " "; readonly text: string }
export interface ToolCardModel {
  readonly title: string;
  readonly arg?: string;
  readonly tone: "running" | "success" | "danger";
  readonly summary: readonly CardLine[];
  readonly diff: readonly DiffLine[];
  /** Lines withheld while collapsed; 0 when expanded or nothing is withheld. */
  readonly hiddenLines: number;
}
export const TOOL_ARG_LIMIT = 60;
export const BASH_PREVIEW_LINES = 3;
export const DIFF_PREVIEW_LINES = 12;
export const CHILD_PREVIEW_LINES = 3;
export function toolTitle(name: string): string;
export function toolCardModel(entry: Extract<TranscriptEntry, { kind: "tool" }>, options: { expanded: boolean }): ToolCardModel;
```
Leave the legacy Transcript renderer and appendChatEvent unchanged.

**Goal** — Add the pure bottom-relative scrolling and follow/unseen state machine.

**Motivation** — The slice 1 acceptance test (brainstorm and spec-review the slice 2 design inside `nax chat`) waits on this redesign.

**Approach** — `viewport.ts`, pure:

`offset` counts lines between the bottom of the view and the last line. The reducer's `total` and `height` arguments are the values before the action; a `content` action carries the new ones. Growth (`action.total - total` when positive) while following keeps `offset` 0; while not following it adds the growth to both `offset` and `unseen`. After every action `offset` is re-clamped against the new total and height; a shrink (for example after `/clear`) never makes `unseen` grow. `pageUp`/`pageDown` move by `height - 1`, `lineUp`/`lineDown` by 1; `offset` is clamped to `[0, max(0, total - height)]`; any move to `offset > 0` sets `follow: false`; reaching `offset 0` sets `follow: true, unseen: 0`. `home` goes to the top, `end` to `INITIAL_VIEWPORT`.

**Scope** — In: pure scrolling reducer/range helpers and unit tests. Out: Ink rendering/keys (US-013), mounting and routing keys in ChatApp (US-020/021). Mouse support (wheel scrolling, click to select) is not added; the screen does not capture the mouse. Searching the transcript and copying from scrolled-off output inside the app are not added; native terminal selection works on what is on screen.

**Interface** —
```ts
export interface ViewportState { readonly offset: number; readonly follow: boolean; readonly unseen: number }
export type ViewportAction =
  | { type: "content"; total: number; height: number }
  | { type: "pageUp" } | { type: "pageDown" } | { type: "lineUp" } | { type: "lineDown" }
  | { type: "home" } | { type: "end" };
export const INITIAL_VIEWPORT: ViewportState; // { offset: 0, follow: true, unseen: 0 }
export function reduceViewport(state: ViewportState, action: ViewportAction, total: number, height: number): ViewportState;
export function visibleRange(total: number, height: number, offset: number): { start: number; end: number };
```

**Goal** — Add the pure code-point-indexed multiline editor reducer.

**Motivation** — The slice 1 acceptance test (brainstorm and spec-review the slice 2 design inside `nax chat`) waits on this redesign.

**Approach** — `line-editor.ts`, a pure reducer over `{ text: string; cursor: number }` (cursor = code-point index into `text`):

Keys: printable input inserts at the cursor (a multi-character chunk, a paste, is inserted whole, `\r\n` and `\r` normalised to `\n`); backspace and `key.delete` both delete before the cursor (ink 6.7 reports the Backspace key's `\u007f` as `delete` and cannot tell it from forward-delete); left/right move one code point; ctrl+a / ctrl+e move to the start / end of the current line; meta+left / meta+right move to the previous / next word boundary; ctrl+u deletes from the line start to the cursor; ctrl+k deletes from the cursor to the line end; ctrl+w deletes the word before the cursor; return with meta or shift inserts `\n`; return when the character before the cursor is `\` replaces that `\` with `\n`; any other return is `submit` with the text (not trimmed); ctrl, escape, tab, up and down are `ignored` (the input component owns them).

**Scope** — In: pure editor state/result types, transformations and cursorRow tests. Out: input component/history/busy/clear-arm behavior (US-015), key ownership integration (US-021). Forward delete (deleting the character under the cursor) is not supported; ink 6.7 reports the Backspace key's `\u007f` and the forward-delete key as the same `delete` key, and both delete before the cursor. Prompt history is not persisted across processes.

**Interface** —
```ts
export interface EditorState { readonly text: string; readonly cursor: number }
export const EMPTY_EDITOR: EditorState;
export type EditorKey = { input: string; key: Pick<Key, "return" | "backspace" | "delete" | "leftArrow" | "rightArrow" | "ctrl" | "meta" | "shift" | "escape" | "tab" | "upArrow" | "downArrow"> };
export type EditorResult = { kind: "edit"; state: EditorState } | { kind: "submit"; text: string } | { kind: "ignored" };
export function editLine(state: EditorState, input: EditorKey): EditorResult;
export function cursorRow(state: EditorState): { row: number; rows: number };
```

**Goal** — Add a pure turn-status reducer and model/token display helpers.

**Motivation** — The slice 1 acceptance test (brainstorm and spec-review the slice 2 design inside `nax chat`) waits on this redesign.

**Approach** — `chat-status.ts`, pure:
- `reduceTurnStatus`: `turn_start` -> running, `startedAt = at`, phase `thinking`, token sums 0, `contextTokens` kept; `thinking_delta` -> `thinking`; `text_delta` -> `writing`; `tool_call` -> `tool` with `toolName`; `tool_result` -> `thinking`; `approval_requested` without `answerable: false` -> `approval`; `approval_resolved` -> `thinking`; `compaction` -> `compacting`; `stream_reset` -> `retrying`; `usage` adds `inputTokens`/`outputTokens` and sets `contextTokens`; `turn_end` -> not running. Events whose `metadata.subagentTask` is set leave the status unchanged.
- `formatTokens`: below 1000 the integer; else one decimal and `k` (`1234` -> `1.2k`).
- `shortModel`: the text after the last `/`; longer than 24 characters -> 23 characters and `…`.

**Scope** — In: TurnStatus/TurnPhase/IDLE_STATUS/reducer/helpers and unit tests. Out: footer (US-017), working line/header/tick constant (US-018), lifecycle/timer mounting (US-020/021). These token values are usage counters, not credentials.

**Interface** —
```ts
export type TurnPhase = "thinking" | "writing" | "tool" | "approval" | "compacting" | "retrying";
export interface TurnStatus {
  readonly running: boolean; readonly startedAt?: string; readonly phase: TurnPhase;
  readonly toolName?: string; readonly inputTokens: number; readonly outputTokens: number;
  /** input + cacheRead + cacheWrite of the latest usage event; survives turn_end. */
  readonly contextTokens?: number;
}
export const IDLE_STATUS: TurnStatus;
export function reduceTurnStatus(status: TurnStatus, event: SessionEvent): TurnStatus;
export function shortModel(model: string): string;
export function formatTokens(n: number): string;
```
